@Paige Ormiston - The user's request is really clear / unambiguous here - and this interaction feels like a a disambiguation pattern. I think there might be some lighter weight interaction options to explore that don't require the user to confirm. For example, I wonder if something more like a 'countdown' / the ghost idea would better suit. 

User: Close this tab
System: Closing now... (with some progress indicator maybe? a bar or circle filling in?) and a "Cancel" button to stop it.

